Add chance-of-precipitation charts to the today and tomorrow pages.

The lower half of both is empty apart from the watermark. This fills it with
hatched probability bars in the same style as the hourly page.

Drawn as inline SVG rather than the canvas + rough.js the hourly page uses: no
script has to run before the screenshot is taken, so the chart cannot come out
half-drawn, and there is nothing to load. It scales to the window's peak with a
floor, and prints the top of scale, because a fixed 0-100% axis makes a 20% day
read as a flat line.

Adds to SimplifiedPage an `_extra_body` hook, so a page can append to the
content section without reimplementing the template, and the shared
`_precip_chart` helper.

`today` uses the existing `hourly_forecasts` (the next nine hours). `tomorrow`
needs hours it does not have, so this adds a `tomorrow_hourly` dataset:
concrete and empty on the base WeatherService, implemented for Open-Meteo,
which already fetches a multi-day hourly array. A provider that cannot reach
that far simply yields no chart rather than breaking the page.

